    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for `POST /api/owners` \u2014 defaulting to the server's current date when omitted, and returning it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, the field is regenerated into both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request input) and `OwnerDto` (response output) as a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (OfficeFloor function) \u2014 After mapping the body to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one; a supplied date passes through unchanged (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Updated the hsqldb seed `data.sql` positional inserts to append a `NULL` (the other DBs use named-column inserts, unaffected by an added nullable column).\n\n**Verification:** The full test suite (`./mvnw -o test`) is green, including both new acceptance tests \u2014 `coreDefaultsToToday` (no date supplied \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (`2020-06-15` preserved).",
